A||N||5||FieroJoe||plug in better throttle response?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||02-27-2001||09:30 PM||||I found this item in the latest summit catalog that I have.  Sounds kinda interesting, what do you guys think?  Will it work, and more importantly, how does it do what it says?  The one pictured should fit most Fieros, except 84's, and the weather-pack connector looks just like the one for the fuel pump/fuel sender located on the fire wall.  I dont know off hand what the TPS connector looks like, is it a 3 conductor weather pack?<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Thingy.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||08:25 AM||||NO NO NO!!! it's an electronic throttle cam! don't do it! Python Remanufacturing the parent company of Venom Performance parts, ADS and JWT have tried this.. none of those products work like they are suposed to. Good idea poor execution. at 1/2 throttle it amplifies the signal that the ECU should be getting (0-1 or 1-5volts make dependant) to "trick it" in to thinking it's at full throttle.. well thats all well and good but delivering the full throttle fuel and not getting the full throttle air of the wide open throttle body will kill your performance, wipe out your cat, cause igniton problems and take $ out of your pocket. Vemon sponcered a couple cars that I have worked on at the shop and on the dyno.. not a single one made more HP/TQ at any rpm on the dyno but 2 wiped out cats due to over fueling and lack of intake charge air.<P><BR>just my $.02||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||02-28-2001||10:13 AM||||Damn, I didnt know that it was so vicious.  I wasnt really thinking of it, I just wondered how the thing worked.  $90 seems kinda steep too.||||reg||13
Z||000003||rockcrawl||02-28-2001||07:49 PM||||I believe it could do what they say, along with all of those other bad things that 1FST2M6 said. If you mashed the throttle every time it might not be so bad!<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||03-01-2001||02:18 AM||||Besides if all it does is amplify the TPS signal then that is the most expensive low power aplifier I have ever seen.<P>You could probably build it from Radio Shack parts for $2 and just as easily destroy your cat.||||reg||1
